text:
A Rodrigón always at odds

with the fawning crowd of pages;

a poor steward who oils himself,

and a damned accountant who brags;


A lady whom idleness adorns,

and others always dressed to the nines in white;

a wrinkled, beetle-browed duenna

who fills the assembly with gossip;


A conjurer who quarrels, steals, and lies,

a cook from this same dough,

a great insolent rabble of liveries;


Much envy, flattery without measure,

and the great lord who serves only

as witness to the vice of his house.
